From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:53:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/39] Servers: a frame cap, an idle frame rate, no web
 plugin, a texture budget

For running without a graphics card, where Mesa's llvmpipe draws in
software and takes every core it's given. Each is a setting, off by
default; Ibasho's tools set them on servers.

- IbashoMaxFPS caps the frame rate. IbashoIdleFPS is a lower cap while no
  LEAP plugin has sent a request for IbashoIdleAfter seconds (after login,
  and not while on autopilot or teleporting); the first request after a
  quiet spell waits up to one idle frame. LLLeap records when the last
  request came.
- IbashoNoWebPlugin: no CEF plugin starts (web pages, web floaters, web
  media on prims), and the web floaters aren't preloaded. Measured on a
  2-CPU container: about 0.55 GB less memory and 30% more frames.
- IbashoTextureBudget: the texture budget in MB, held as given. The
  viewer's own budget comes from the reported video memory, which llvmpipe
  reports as the system's RAM, and has a 768 MB floor.
